From 31f1b4e08904353de3fa4103b0d033c33ff3b1bd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Majid Arasskhani <M.Arasskhani@gosilkroad.net>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 15:12:21 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 03/22] fix(chat): fence web, document and learned-memory text
 as untrusted in the default chat path
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Bug: only the Agent path wrapped retrieved content in UNTRUSTED markers and
stated a runtime policy. Default chat pasted fetched pages, search snippets,
project resource excerpts and auto-learned memory straight into the system
prompt, so a page saying "ignore your instructions" spoke with the same
authority as the operator. The Agent path also kept its own copy of the
policy text and markers, so the two were already drifting.

Change: app/core/prompt_fences.py is the single implementation
(RUNTIME_POLICY, wrap_untrusted(label, text, source=), untrusted_preamble).
wrap_untrusted neutralises a payload's own BEGIN/END markers so a page cannot
close the fence early. chat_tools_service fences search results and each
fetched page (including fetch failures) and puts the policy first whenever
any tool block is present; project_turn_planner fences resource excerpts and
leads with the policy; project memory fences the chat-learned facts (manual
facts saved by members stay plain); agent_prompt_service imports the shared
policy and wrappers instead of its own copies.

Tests: tests/test_prompt_fences.py — marker neutralisation, policy precedes
the first fence, every occurrence of an injected string sits inside a fence,
fetch failures fenced, Agent path uses the shared module.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
